WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W19 (0.2.5)


STATE

  Version 0.2.5, Phase P3 COMPLETE (line editor, shared O_APPEND
  history, POSIX job control, completion, syntax highlighting &
  suggestions, and prompts/hooks), on branch dev. 0.2.5 adds:
  - safe prompt escape expansion in include/tam-clam/prompt.h and
    src/prompt.c (\u, \h, \H, \w, \W, \$, \?, \j, \t, \T, \A, \d, \s,
    \v, \n, \r, \e, \\, \[/\]; never re-parsed as code, zero timers);
  - right-aligned RPS1 / RPROMPT in src/edit/render.c (auto-hides when
    buffer approaches, transient on Enter);
  - precmd / PROMPT_COMMAND before each prompt and preexec ($1=cmd) /
    PS0 before each command (preserving $?);
  - tests/test_prompt.c unit tests, live PTY prompt/hook tests in
    tests/pty/test_pty.c, and sandbox/demo-0.2.5-prompts.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


